{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1291114-heirs-to-creation-an-exalted-3e-pbp-interest-check","id":1291114,"title":"Heirs to Creation - An Exalted 3e PbP Interest Check","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-23T06:28:58-08:00","id":1291114,"title":"Heirs to Creation - An Exalted 3e PbP Interest Check","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Intro</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Dun-lat is a satrapy roughly a hundred miles south of the southern end of the Steaming Sea, on the route between Ember and the Varangian City-States. Centered on the River Ammon, called the Mother River, Dun-lat is a devout satrapy of the Realm, where every couple considers it their religious duty to give their firstborn to the Immaculate Order as future monks, meaning that the Order has an incredibly powerful presence in Dun-lat. Ruled for nearly three hundred years by House Tepet, Dun-lat is home to incredibly valuable salt mines, great sandstone quarries, tombs of an ancient dynasty, and a forgotten manse that was once a sanctuary in the desert.<br /> In recent years, Dun-lat has begun its descent into total chaos, as half a year ago, a revolutionary of uncertain origin claiming to be the daughter of the Mother River began to strike against the forces of House Tepet, harrying and destroying them almost unto the point of defeat until she was killed in battle. Now the neighboring satrapies look hungrily on as bandits roam the countryside and former rebels plot to overthrow House Tepet once and for all. In the shadows, the eyes of ambitious spirits and mysterious Exalts converge on the slowly collapsing kingdom, each with their own agenda. Into this chaos, the Solars return, their footsteps shaking the entirety of Dun-lat... and beyond.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Hello there! I'm *End, and I'm a longtime member of these lovely forums, though I've been absent for many a year, recently. In any case, I'd like to check in on potential interest in playing Solars in the South - not <i>quite</i> the Southeast, but definitely the eastern part of the Southern Threshold. House Tepet and its stooges in power are losing their grip on their diverse kingdom, while rebels and bandits alike torment the countryside.<br /> <br /> I'm looking for a perfect circle, both because I plan to try to use Solar XP, and because I tend to like the symmetry it offers. That means I'd like 5 players, with possible allowances for players seeking to play other splats - though I know Lunars isn't out in its fullest extent yet, and DBs are less than likely to ally with Solars, that is an option I'm willing to entertain, if not <i>eager</i> to do so. Anyways, this is mostly just looking for people to express an interest in this.<br /> <br /> The format would be play-by-post. I usually use Google Docs for that, but I'm willing to do other things, if the demand is high enough. Anyways, hope to hear back from interested parties soon, and thanks in advance for reading!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1ny-IC9WU2WbQd3ILAW6ez5LpirfAYWfQ?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a set of setting documents that I, uh, may have gone overboard with. &gt;_&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>All that I write but don't cite is simply my perspective, colored by my experiences and beliefs. I extrapolate a lot, too, so don't take it too seriously. :P","edited":{"userid":7858,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","user":"*End","date":". 02-23-2019, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7858-end","name":"*End","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7858_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T06:46:29-08:00","id":1291117,"title":"","content":"Hi! I'm always up for Exalted games, and I already have characters lying around for most of the castes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T07:16:52-08:00","id":1291121,"title":"","content":"I've been looking for an outlet for Exalted and would be interested (my table top group is currently playing Scion but with Lunars coming out, it's got me reading through my Exalted books again). I've played all the castes at one point or another and could again, but I tend to prefer Twilight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4637-demonchilde","name":"demonchilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-23T07:41:42-08:00","id":1291125,"title":"","content":"PBP Exalted? Count me as interested, I have concepts for most castes flying around somewhere!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-ka